cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Gauge Neural Dynamics: Learning Context-Dependent Coordinate Systems in Biological Neural Representations"
message: "If you use this software or the framework, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chandra"
    given-names: "Sunkalp"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sunkalpchandra/gauge-neural-dynamics"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational neuroscience
  - neural manifolds
  - Lie groups
  - gauge theory
  - hippocampal remapping
  - grid cells
  - motor cortex
  - persistent homology
abstract: >-
  A framework in which context-dependent neural representations are modelled as a
  shared latent state read out through a context-dependent gauge transformation,
  x_c = f(T_c(z)), with T_c the exponential of a context-dependent element of a
  learned finite-dimensional Lie algebra. Identity and exact invertibility follow
  from the construction; closure under composition is measured rather than
  assumed. Includes simulations of hippocampal remapping, grid-cell phase
  translation and a trained reaching network, four metrics for context-dependent
  geometry, and a proof that a single-chart gauge field cannot cover a cyclic
  context variable.
